course: dictionary
lesson: 8907
title: Shuttle: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A shuttle is something or someone that goes back and forth between two places, again and again. «The shuttle bus runs every ten minutes between the airport and the car park.» The word bus tells you what kind of shuttle it is, and back and forth tells you what it does.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. «The space shuttle flew into space and landed back on Earth like a plane.» Here shuttle is a spacecraft. In badminton, the shuttle is the feathered object you hit over the net. In weaving, it is the tool that carries thread across the loom. Context tells you which meaning to pick.
explain: Shuttle can also be a verb, meaning to go or carry people between places many times. «Her dad and mum shuttle her between two homes each week.» Here shuttle is an action, and the clue is between two homes. When a word could be a thing or an action, ask yourself: is someone doing something, or is it a thing?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Shuttle can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: A shuttle bus goes back and forth between two places, often.
fact: A space shuttle was a spacecraft that could fly into space, land on Earth like a plane, and be used again.
fact: In badminton, a shuttle is the feathered object you hit over the net.
exercise: What is the shuttle in «The shuttle bus runs every ten minutes between the airport and the car park.»? | A long, slow train to the seaside | *A bus that goes back and forth between two places | A plant that grows at airports | A type of car park
exercise: In badminton, what is the shuttle? | A player who runs between the goals | *A feathered object you hit over the net | A net stretched across the court | A racket with a long handle
exercise: «Her dad and mum shuttle her between two homes each week.» What does shuttle mean here? | To buy a new home | *To go back and forth between places many times | To stay in one place all week | To cook a meal together
test: «The space shuttle could fly into space and land back on Earth, so it could be used again.» Why could it be used again? | *It could land and fly again | It only ever flew once | It was made of wood | It was a shuttle bus
test: Maya says shuttle must mean a bus in every sentence. Is she right? | *No, shuttle can be a spacecraft, a shuttlecock, or a verb meaning to go back and forth | Yes, shuttle always means bus | No, shuttle is never a thing | Yes, because it is in the bus timetable
exam: In «The weaver pushed the shuttle across the loom», what is a shuttle? | *A tool that carries thread across a loom | A feathered ball you hit over a net | A type of train | A small boat
